\details{
Wraps the ESPN core-v2 season athlete index
\code{sports.core.api.espn.com/v2/sports/football/leagues/college-football/seasons/{year}/teams/{team_id}/athletes}.
The index returns one \verb{$ref} per athlete; this wrapper dereferences each
athlete resource and flattens it into a row. The site-v2 roster endpoint
is deliberately \strong{not} used: it returns only the team's \emph{current}
roster and silently ignores a \code{season} query parameter, so it cannot
deliver historical rosters. The core-v2 path used here is genuinely
season-scoped.

Because each athlete is dereferenced individually, a full roster is
roughly 150-220 HTTP requests; allow a few seconds per call.

When \code{team_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN team catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_teams]{espn_cfb_teams()}}) is fetched once and friendly team fields are joined
in next to the \code{team_id} column -- \code{team_name}, \code{team_abbreviation},
\code{team_location}, \code{team_display_name}, \code{team_short_display_name},
\code{team_nickname}, \code{team_color}, \code{team_alternate_color},
\code{team_logo_href}, and \code{team_logo_dark_href}, inserted immediately after
\code{team_id}. A catalog failure degrades to \code{NA} rather than erroring the
wrapper. Set \code{team_detail = FALSE} to skip the catalog fetch and the
join.

When \code{position_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN position catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_positions]{espn_cfb_positions()}}) is fetched once and joined onto the
\code{position_id} column, appending the five \verb{position_*} detail columns
(\code{position_name}, \code{position_display_name}, \code{position_abbreviation},
\code{position_leaf}, \code{position_parent_id}). A catalog failure degrades to
\code{NA} rather than erroring the wrapper. Set \code{position_detail = FALSE} to
skip the extra fetch and the join.
}
